Now that got me, so I googled around to answer my own questions.

I found out that there were some problems in creating r.g.r.n. because
originally it was to replace rec.games.hack.

When net.games.hack (is this the reason that NH is called that with
net.*.hack ?) was created there was this post:

From: Gene Spafford (spaf@gatech.UUCP)
Subject: net.games.hack is created
Newsgroups: net.news.group, net.games, net.games.rogue, net.games.hack
Date: 1985-01-17 09:43:33 PST

The first proposal concerning the creation of r.g.r.n. is to be found here:

From: Andrew Solovay (solovay@netcom.com)
Subject: 2nd RFD: rec.games.roguelike.* hierarchy
Newsgroups: news.announce.newgroups, news.groups, rec.games.hack,
rec.games.rogue, rec.games.moria, alt.games.omega, rec.games.misc
Date: 1993-07-12 17:55:13 PST

A vote was organized but r.g.r.n. was voted against:

From: Andrew Solovay (solovay@netcom.com)
Subject: RESULT: rec.games.roguelike reorganization
Newsgroups: news.announce.newgroups, news.groups, rec.games.hack,
rec.games.rogue, rec.games.moria, alt.games.omega, rec.games.misc
Date: 1993-08-18 07:20:03 PST

A year later the topic was brought up again:

From: Jay Maynard (jmaynard@admin5.hsc.uth.tmc.edu)
Subject: CFV: rec.games.roguelike.{moria,nethack,rogue}
Newsgroups: news.announce.newgroups, news.groups,
rec.games.roguelike.announce, rec.games.moria, rec.games.hack,
rec.games.rogue, rec.games.roguelike.angband, rec.games.roguelike.misc
Date: 1994-05-09 17:54:03 PST

And this time all concerned groups passed the vote:

From: Jay Maynard (jmaynard@admin5.hsc.uth.tmc.edu)
Subject: RESULT: rec.games.roguelike.{moria,nethack,rogue} all groups pass
Newsgroups: news.announce.newgroups, news.groups,
rec.games.roguelike.announce, rec.games.moria, rec.games.hack,
rec.games.rogue, rec.games.roguelike.angband, rec.games.roguelike.misc
Date: 1994-06-01 13:31:48 PST

